[N 45-47 Tanaris]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Menethil to Theramore by boat, Theramore to Gadgetzan by air (bind). The Explorers' League at the Uldum pedestal, the Dunemaul compound and Marvon's Gahz'ridian ornaments, the Noxious Lair and the silithid chain, Thistleshrub Valley and Tooga's walk home to Torta, the Egg-O-Matic hand-in. Handle With Care and Rise of the Silithid go on to Darnassus.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 47|r  -  this chapter wants level 47 for its mobs: Dunemaul ogres 46-48 and Gor'marok 49, the Centipaar of the Noxious Lair and the Hazzali of the Gaping Chasm 47-50, Thistleshrub Valley 48-50. Every quest here can be taken at 45 (The Stone Watcher, Seeing What Happens and Thistleshrub Valley need 45, the rest 39-44). The legs run lowest first: the Dunemaul compound and the ornaments, then the Uldum pedestal (talk only, but level 48-49 elite Dune Smashers stand beside it), then the Noxious Lair, Thistleshrub Valley with Tooga, and the Gaping Chasm last. Under 46: kill Gor'marok last in the compound and pull the Thistleshrub Rootshapers (49-50) one at a time
[OC]|cffffffffTanaris|r  -  you start at Menethil Harbor after chapter 52 with hearth = Ironforge and bind Gadgetzan on arrival. About 41,600 quest XP on the eleven plain quests (37,400 without the Hippogryph Egg) and 1g 95s of quest money; every giver, hand-in and mob position comes from the DB, the roads do not
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Seeing What Happens (2946, with the Miniature Platinum Discs, from Historian Karnik in chapter 52) goes to the Uldum pedestal. The Super Egg-O-Matic (2741, taken in chapter 46) is handed in with the Hippogryph Egg from Feralas (chapter 50). Arcane Runes (3449) rides on to Azshara (chapter 55). Clamlette Surprise (6610) if you took it in chapter 46
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Training:|r no shaman trainer in Dustwallow or Tanaris; the next ranks wait for Ironforge in chapter 57

